## 9. Methods Paper Outline

The experimental validation in Section 7 directly feeds into a methods paper. Proposed structure:

**Title:** FindSimilarity: Quantifying Inter-Cluster Distances and Condition-Specific Divergence in Single-Cell Latent Spaces

**Abstract:** UMAPs don't preserve global distances; we present a framework that quantifies distances in latent space, supporting multiple metrics, condition-stratified analysis, and statistical testing.

**Introduction:** Motivation (the UMAP global distance problem), gap analysis (Section 2 of this document), and a brief overview of the framework.

**Methods:** API design, distance metrics (mathematical definitions), permutation testing framework, implementation details.

**Results:**

- Benchmarking distance metrics on known cell type relationships (Experiment 3).
- Variance weighting and dimension selection (Experiments 1–2).
- Wasserstein approximation comparison (Experiment 4).
- Condition-specific divergence detection (Experiment 10) — the key biological result.
- Scalability (Experiment 11).

**Discussion:** Recommendations for when to use each metric, limitations (assumptions about latent space quality), relationship to PAGA and other tools, future directions (multi-modal, spatial).

**Data and Code Availability:** All code as a Seurat PR + standalone R package. Simulation scripts and analysis notebooks on GitHub.

