## 10. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Seurat maintainers reject the PR scope | High | Engage early with Seurat team. Alternatively, release as a standalone package (SeuratSimilarity) that extends Seurat objects via S3 methods. |
| Distribution methods too slow for large datasets | Medium | Implement per-cluster subsampling (e.g., max 1000 cells per cluster). Benchmark early (Experiment 11). |
| No single method dominates across all scenarios | Low | This is actually expected and is a feature: document which method suits which question. The paper becomes stronger as a comparative guide. |
| Permutation testing computationally prohibitive | Medium | Offer analytic p-values for MMD (asymptotic distribution is known). Use permutations only where needed. |
| Biological validation is ambiguous (no absolute ground truth for real data) | Medium | Combine simulated data (known ground truth) with real data (known biology). Use multiple real datasets. Focus on relative ordering, not absolute values. |

